      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #93): a fix-time-only error (one that never
      ⍝ gets to execute at all, e.g. "1)" -- unbalanced parenthesis)
      ⍝ used to leave ⎕ET/⎕EM reporting whatever the *previous*
      ⍝ statement's run-time error had been, since neither
      ⍝ Token_string::all_brackets_closed() nor
      ⍝ Error::throw_parse_error() ever stored the new error where
      ⍝ ⎕ET/⎕EM look for it (StateIndicator::get_error()) -- only
      ⍝ run-time errors (via throw_apl_error()) did that.
